# Generated API docs

The [generated API reference](https://benomahony.github.io/zig-typesafe-ai/api/) lists every public
declaration with its doc comment. To build it locally with Zig's autodoc:

```sh
zig build docs
python3 -m http.server -d zig-out/docs/api
```

# Examples

The `examples/` directory contains three programs. Each needs `TYPESAFE_API_KEY`.

| Command | Shows |
| --- | --- |
| `zig build run-triage -- "message"` | The typed DSL: noul with criteria, choice from a struct and from an enum, score, and `Diagnostics` |
| `zig build run-dynamic -- "text" label...` | Runtime-built questions with `systemOne` |
| `zig build run-models` | `listModels` |

# Mapping to the HTTP API

| HTTP | tai |
| --- | --- |
| `POST /v1/systemone` | `Client.ask` (typed) and `Client.systemOne` (runtime) |
| `GET /v1/models` | `Client.listModels` |
| `Authorization: Bearer` | `Options.api_key` / `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` |
| `state` | The first argument of `ask`, or `Request.state` |
| `questions.{id}` | A struct field name, or `NamedQuestion.name` |
| noul `criteria.true` / `.false` | `.criteria(yes, no)` |
| choice `criteria` map | Struct literal or enum type |
| score `criteria` array | Tuple, struct literal, or enum type |
| `answers.{id}` | `r.answers.{field}` or `Response.get(id)` |
| `usage` | `r.usage` |

# Running the tests

```sh
zig build test
```

The suite includes unit tests for serialization and parsing, plus tests
against a local mock HTTP server. Those cover retries, `Retry-After`, error
statuses, headers and connection failures, and need no network access or API
key.
